{"archetypes":[{"name":"stale-term-coverage","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan is itself a residual-cleanup after three issues were closed; the key risk is that the grep scope missed additional stale-phrase sites in the same edit-in-sync closure graph.","prompt_body":"The plan claims a `grep -i amend` sweep across the bump/drop-bump/CHANGELOG pathway surfaced exactly two residual sites. Verify that this sweep was exhaustive: check sibling `.md` files for every script in the bump+drop-bump+CHANGELOG pathway (e.g., `scripts/commit-changelog.md`, `scripts/drop-bump-commit.md`, `.claude/skills/bump-version/scripts/*.md`, `scripts/conflict-resolution.md`) for any remaining references to 'amend', 'git-amend-add', or 'amended bump' that the plan explicitly excluded or may have missed. For each exclusion the plan names (CHANGELOG.md historical entries, git-amend-add.md), confirm the rationale is sound: is the site truly immutable/historical, or is it a live contract line that should also be updated? Also verify that the exact before-text phrases the plan quotes ('on the path that doesn't amend' and 'CHANGELOG detection/amend') actually appear verbatim in the cited files at the stated line numbers, since an Edit-tool collision with an already-resolved phrase would silently skip the replacement. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
